Description:
The Music of Carl Stalling, Scott Bradley, Raymond Scott and more
Drummer Stu Brown&nbsp;premieres a brand new set of music celebrating the work of the great&nbsp;cartoon composers of the 20th Century. Stu&rsquo;s critically acclaimed&nbsp;sextet album, Twisted Toons &ndash; The Music of Raymond&nbsp;Scott,&nbsp;was one of Mojo Magazines top 10 jazz releases of 2009 and he now&nbsp;returns with scores by Carl Stalling (Looney&nbsp;Tunes) Scott Bradley (Tom &amp; Jerry/Tex Avery), and Scott.
This is a rare opportunity to experience it up close&nbsp;and in person in all its madcap glory. Put on your&nbsp;ACME Rocket&nbsp;Boots and get ready for an eye-popping ride&hellip;
'Highly enjoyable' 4* Scotsman review&nbsp;

With Evan Christopher, Duke Heitger, Don Vappie
A special concert, marking the tenth anniversary of this great Scottish jazz institution. Their first concert featured Morton&rsquo;s music, and now, Mathieson presents rarely heard &ndash; in a couple of cases, perhaps never heard before &ndash; unpublished Big Band scores, made available from the archives of HNOC in New Orleans. A specially enhanced Orchestra as been put together to play this music in the second half of the concert: Kevin Ferris, Billy Hunter and Duke Heitger (tpts), Evan Christopher (cl); Dick Lee, Martin Foster (as), Konrad Wiszniewski (ts), Allon Beauvoisin (ts,bars), Chris Greive (lead), Phil O'Malley&nbsp;&amp;&nbsp;Michael Owers (tb), Tom Finlay (p), Don Vappie (gtr/bjo), Roy Percy (b) and Ken Mathieson (dms/arr). In the first half, the CJO with their New Orleans guests, will play small group music by Morton and others. A fitting tribute to the greatest composer of early jazz, and to our own CJO.

With gratitude to Daniel Hammer and The Historic New Orleans Collection at the University of New Orleans for their generosity and support of this project&nbsp;

Venue description:
Jupiter Artland is a unique, award winning sculpture garden 12 miles outside Edinburgh which houses the private art collection of Robert and Nicky Wilson. Jupiter Artland is a registered charity and the Foundation is committed to nurturing the work of outstanding contemporary artists. 

Since 2009 Jupiter has commissioned more than 30 site-specific works by top-class international artists. Artworks on permanent display in the peaceful woodland and meadows of the Jacobean house include major pieces by leading contemporary sculptors including Nathan Coley, Ian Hamilton Finlay, Laura Ford, Anya Gallaccio, Andy Goldsworthy, Antony Gormley, Charles Jencks, Anish Kapoor, Jim Lambie, Peter Liversidge, Cornelia Parker, Marc Quinn and Shane Waltener.
@jupiterartland

Easter Road Billboard, EH7 5QJ
@EdArtFest
#wheredoiend

The exhibition will take place in a traditional Victorian Glasshouse within the grounds of Edinburgh’s Lauriston Castle. The castle is situated just outside Edinburgh, three miles from the centre of town. It is set in thirty acres of parkland and formal gardens with views overlooking the Firth of Forth.
please contact emma pratt via mail@emmapratt.co.uk for any queries regarding this exhibition

